      "text": "I've worn hearing aids for about six years now, and the thing nobody told me at the start was how long it takes your brain to settle in. The first two weeks were rough. Everything sounded tinny and I kept turning them off at dinner. My audiologist said to wear them all day anyway, even when it's annoying, and I'm glad I listened. By week five the clatter faded into the background. If you're new and it feels awful, that's normal. Give it a month before you decide they don't work for you.",
